The '''2006 Football League Cup final''' also known as the '''2006 Carling Cup final''' for sponsorship reasons, was played between [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] and [[Wigan Athletic F.C.|Wigan Athletic]] on 26 February 2006. Manchester United won the match comfortably, by four goals to nil. [[Louis Saha]] and [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] both scored one goal, and [[Wayne Rooney]] scored twice. For the trophy presentation, the Manchester United players wore special shirts reading "For You Smudge", referring to [[Alan Smith (footballer born 1980)|Alan Smith]], who had broken his left leg during a recent [[FA Cup]] match against [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/league_cup/4752806.stm |title=Carling Cup final clockwatch |date=26 February 2006 |access-date=16 August 2014 |publisher=BBC}}</ref> Wigan goalkeeper [[Mike Pollitt]] picked up a hamstring injury after just 14 minutes, cutting short a dream cup final for the [[Journeyman (sports)#Association football|journeyman]] player, who started his career with the Red Devils.
